    ":question/id": "1da25f7d-182b-5d2d-b5c8-9d3f66bb445c",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104703",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{121}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we note that $\\sqrt{121}=11$ is a natural number, so it belongs to $N.$\n\nSince every natural number is also an integer number, $\\sqrt{121}$ also belongs to $Z.$ \n\nOn the other hand, the sets ${Z}^{-}$ and ${Q}^{-}$ only contain negative numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{121}$ does not belong to either of these sets. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$N$ (natural numbers)\u201d; \u201c$Z$ (integers)\u201d only."
  },
