    ":question/id": "e51e86f2-eaf4-5f67-aebb-f55a23118243",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-181544",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\pi $ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The number $-\\pi $ is not a rational number. Consequently, $-\\pi $ does not belong to any of the sets  ${Q}^{-}$ nor $Q.$\n\nHowever, $-\\pi $ is a real number, so it belongs to $R.$\n\nFinally, since every real number is also a complex number, $-\\pi $ also belongs to $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$R$ (real numbers)\u201d; \u201c$C$ (complex numbers)\u201d only."
  },
