    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-181545",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The number $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ is not an integer nor a rational number. Consequently, $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ does not belong to any of the sets $Z,$ ${Q}^{+},$ nor $Q.$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ is a real number, so it belongs to $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$R$ (real numbers)\u201d only."
  },
