    ":question/id": "4fc9ff9e-591c-5172-b83a-e2856d63bd94",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-36248",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the positive integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The positive integer numbers are $1,2,3,\u2026$\n\n- Since all positive integer numbers are natural numbers, all the positive integers belong to $N.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\n- Since all positive integer numbers are positive real numbers, all the positive integer numbers belong to ${R}^{+}.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, positive integer numbers as, for instance, $2$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the positive integer numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, positive integer numbers as, for instance, $2$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the positive integer numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$N$ (natural numbers)\u201d; ${R}^{+}$ only."
  },
