    ":question/id": "cedbe49b-bcb9-5d4b-9edb-8a333a5510e3",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-37315",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\sqrt{81}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Note that $-\\sqrt{81}=-9.$ Therefore $-\\sqrt{81}$ is a negative integer. So it's in the sets $Z,$ ${Z}_{0}^{-},$ and ${Z}^{-}.$ \n\nMoreover, since every integer is also a real number, $-\\sqrt{81}$ also belongs to $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$Z$ (integers)\u201d; ${Z}^{-}$; ${Z}_{0}^{-}$; \u201c$R$ (real numbers)\u201d."
  },
