    ":question/id": "17cf8bd5-1b50-5ea6-9196-c8cc3bb865c7",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-36246",
    ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the negative integers belong?\n\nI. $Z$\n\nII. ${Z}^{+}$\n\nIII. ${Q}^{+}$\n\nIV. ${Q}^{-}$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The negative integers are $-1,-2,-3,\u2026$\n\n- Since all negative integers are integer numbers, all the negative integers belong to $Z.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\n- The set ${Z}^{+}$ contains all the positive integer numbers. However, negative integer numbers as, for instance, $-2$ don't belong to ${Z}^{+},$ so ${Z}^{+}$ does *not* contain the negative integer numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\n- The set ${Q}^{+}$ contains all the positive rational numbers. However, negative integer numbers as, for instance, $-2$ don't belong to ${Q}^{+},$ so ${Q}^{+}$ does *not* contain the negative integer numbers. $\\,\\times$\n\n- Since all the negative integer numbers are negative rational numbers, all the negative integer numbers belong to ${Q}^{-}.$ $\\,\u2713$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""
